# Fork a working “complete thing”

Steve’s layman model: systems like BoardsToPrice are one black box (input → usable output / text link). He does not distinguish staging vs harness vs notify unless we say so.

## Before coding a sibling / fork

In plain language, state:

1. **Must stay identical end-to-end** (customer outcome parity): e.g. photo rename before detect, harness pages, one success text, preview thumb, fail/retry policy, retention prune.
2. **Intentionally different** (only the new feature): e.g. named folders → slug in the URL.
3. **One real-world acceptance test** both paths must pass: same ugly Lexi inputs (iPhone UUID JPG names, HEIC if relevant) through the original and the fork → publish + single success text.

Do not treat “duplicate the middle engine” as “duplicate the complete thing.” Staging and notify are part of the product.

## Prefer shared helpers over drifting copies

When two watchers should behave the same before/after the shared engine, share one helper (e.g. stage boards like BoardsToPrice) rather than rewriting staging in each script.

## Related

CollectionsToPrice was meant as BoardsToPrice + folder names. Missing Boards staging rename caused the UUID harness failure; dual notify caused double texts. See overnight lessons in chat / NamedCollectionsPricing README.
